  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 216 AM CDT Sat Oct 17 2026\n\nLittle change is seen among the most recent model initializations \ncompared to the forecasts over the last 24 hours. With nearly steady \ntroughing over the western CONUS and upper-level ridging southeast \nof the Middle Mississippi Valley, the CWA will be beneath \nsouthwesterly flow. This flow will be weak due to a slack pressure \ngradient aloft, with little in the way of warm air advection or \npassing disturbances. This translates to a gradual warming trend \nwith little to no chance for rain through Saturday. While confidence \nis high that temperatures will be above normal by mid-week, \nconfidence in specific values is still low. The NBM and its bias-\ncorrected components are warmer than a majority of ensemble guidance \nat this point, with its solution favoring highs in the low to mid \n80s by the end of the week. This is nearly 5-10 degrees above the \n75th percentile of ensemble guidance, but is still within the \nenvelope of reasonable outcomes. Therefore, adjustments will not be \nmade to the forecast until lead time and ensemble spread decrease \nfurther.",
